{"name":"University of Tennessee Orange","hex":"#f77f00","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"university","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An institution of higher education that provides facilities for teaching, research, and the conferral of academic degrees across undergraduate, graduate, and often professional levels.","The entirety of a group; all members of a class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/university"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tennessee Orange","blocks":[{"text":"\"Tennessee Orange\" is a song by American country music singer Megan Moroney. The song was released in December 2022 as her debut single and the lead single from her debut studio album Lucky. Moroney wrote the song with Ben Williams, David Fanning, and Paul Jenkins."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/44/Megan_Moroney_-_Tennessee_Orange.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennessee_Orange"},{"title":"University of Tennessee","blocks":[{"text":"The University of Tennessee, Knoxville is a public land-grant research university in Knoxville, Tennessee, United States. Founded in 1794, two years before Tennessee became the 16th state, it is the flagship campus of the University of Tennessee system, with 14 colleges. It hosts more than 30,000 students from all 50 states and more than 100 foreign countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/55/Seal_of_the_University_of_Tennessee.svg/330px-Seal_of_the_University_of_Tennessee.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Tennessee"},{"title":"University","blocks":[{"text":"A university is an institution of tertiary education and research which awards academic degrees in several academic disciplines. University is derived from the Latin phrase universitas magistrorum et scholarium, which roughly means \"community of teachers and scholars\". Universities typically offer both undergraduate and postgraduate programs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Columbia_University%2C_NYC_%28June_2014%29_-_09.JPG/330px-Columbia_University%2C_NYC_%28June_2014%29_-_09.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University"},{"title":"Tennessee","blocks":[{"text":"Tennessee, officially the State of Tennessee, is a landlocked state in the Southeastern region of the United States. It borders Kentucky to the north, Virginia to the northeast, North Carolina to the east, Georgia, Alabama, and Mississippi to the south, Arkansas to the southwest, and Missouri to the northwest. Tennessee is the 36th-largest by area and the 15th-most populous of the 50 states. According to the United States Census Bureau, the state's estimated population as of 2024 is 7.22 million."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Flag_of_Tennessee.svg/330px-Flag_of_Tennessee.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennessee"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/The_Hill_at_UT_Knoxville_in_the_1800s.jpg/330px-The_Hill_at_UT_Knoxville_in_the_1800s.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu